  "assessment": [
    "November was an interaction pass, not a rebuild. Every one of the 20 decks changed, but most swaps trade greedy cards (Pot of Desires and Prosperity, Card Scanner, Upstart Goblin) and Ghost Belle for hand traps and board breakers. Only Synchron, Runick, Lunalight and Gren Maju changed how they actually play.",
    "The result is a collection that is much better at going second without getting any less consistent. The top five didn't move. The gains landed mid-table: Runick Typhoon, Primite Blue-Eyes and Blackwing Angelechy each climbed three places, and White Forest two."
  ],
  "watch": "Still the soft spots: Ryu-Ge Mitsurugi and Lunalight have the fewest interaction pieces (9 each), and Dinomorphia, Ryu-Ge and Lunalight are only 15% to see a breaker going second.",
